{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/353813-2ed-hack-milestones-as-aspirations","id":353813,"title":"2ed Hack - Milestones as Aspirations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-29T09:58:27-08:00","id":353813,"title":"2ed Hack - Milestones as Aspirations","content":"As I prepare the 1.5 ed game ( Promethean 1ed game with some 2ed hacks and GMC rules as base ) I got, I think, cool idea for little Pilgrimage mechanics in spirit of nWoD 2ed. It is totally fan based, but I would be honored if devs would use it on <b>PtC 2ed</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i><b>Personal Milestones Hack</b></i><br /> <br /> Idea is simple: <b>Prometheans get a special 3 Aspirations on their sheet that are Milestones</b> - as werewolves get they Pack Aspirations and mages get their Obsessions.<br /> <br /> <b>Rules:</b> <i>Player</i> can choose up to 3 Milestones he wants his character to experience on Pilgrimage, that follow the rules of other Aspirations, but generate Vitriol Beats for fulfilling. Still, Storyteller makes his main Milestones list for each Player's Character. One of those three Milestones slots must be used for <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/playing-at-humanity-roles-promethean-the-created/\" target=\"_blank\">Role</a>'s Milestones. If player chosen and fulfilled Milestone is the same as the one on Storytellers list, Milestone on the list is erased and character cannot choose or undergone the same Milestone twice.<br /> <br /> Do you like it? Is it need more tweaking? What are your thoughts on this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-31-2014, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T21:48:55-08:00","id":355459,"title":"","content":"Dang, I really wish Milestones had won out in last week's blog vote!<br /> <br /> I think this is a solid start to a good &quot;1.5&quot; ruleset, and I'd be willing to bet we'll see something akin to Aspirations like this in 2e. I do have a few questions that I hope will help sharpen the idea for your players.<br /> <br /> 1) What makes a Personal Milestone (which is what I'm dubbing your hack, here) different from an Aspiration? Can you give us some good examples?<br /> <br /> 2) Is the Promethean aware of the Milestones their player selects, are they aware of some of them, or are they aware of none of them?<br /> <br /> 3) Does the player choose another Milestone when one of theirs is fulfilled, aside from the one reserved for the Role? (You get one Milestone per Role, it would seem)<br /> <br /> My only other comment is that if the player and the Storyteller choose the same Milestone, the burden of coming up with another Milestone should fall squarely on the Storyteller's shoulders if they think another is necessary. It gives the player more agency in the game and over their character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T23:37:01-08:00","id":355510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/353813-2ed-hack-milestones-as-aspirations?p=355459#post355459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) What makes a Personal Milestone (which is what I'm dubbing your hack, here) different from an Aspiration? Can you give us some good examples?</div> </div> </div> </div>Idea for hack name stolen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As <b>GMC </b>is definine it, Aspirations are things a <i>player</i> wants for his character to expirance. It goes with example of character confronting with the ghost, even if character would be frightened by it. I see Personal Milestones as a like, but with bend of &quot;personal development&quot; of chracter. Very good examples would be from Roles spoiler above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/353813-2ed-hack-milestones-as-aspirations?p=355459#post355459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Is the Promethean aware of the Milestones their player selects, are they aware of some of them, or are they aware of none of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think mostly the Prometheans will be aware of their Milestones - most of the time were the thing the Created wanted to expiriance. Like &quot;I would want to get close with child, as I'm on Aurum&quot; - things like this.<br /> <br /> The character would probably do not know on things like Personal Milestone as &quot;Confront with inner fear&quot; - character with fear of fire probably would do not want to get near it, but player thinks it's major character development moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/353813-2ed-hack-milestones-as-aspirations?p=355459#post355459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Does the player choose another Milestone when one of theirs is fulfilled, aside from the one reserved for the Role? (You get one Milestone per Role, it would seem)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, just like normal Aspirations. And yes, as you choose only one Role at the time, you can only choose one Personal Milestone for one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/353813-2ed-hack-milestones-as-aspirations?p=355459#post355459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only other comment is that if the player and the Storyteller choose the same Milestone, the burden of coming up with another Milestone should fall squarely on the Storyteller's shoulders if they think another is necessary. It gives the player more agency in the game and over their character.</div> </div> </div> </div>it was my idea from the begining. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T07:55:53-08:00","id":355759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/353813-2ed-hack-milestones-as-aspirations?p=355510#post355510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think mostly the Prometheans will be aware of their Milestones - most of the time were the thing the Created wanted to expiriance. Like &quot;I would want to get close with child, as I'm on Aurum&quot; - things like this.<br /> <br /> The character would probably do not know on things like Personal Milestone as &quot;Confront with inner fear&quot; - character with fear of fire probably would do not want to get near it, but player thinks it's major character development moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, since milestones generate Vitriol, they imply an alchemical reaction taking place inside the Promethean - which in turn could imply she'd feel something when she approaches them, most likely a feeling she'd learn to recognise. That aside, I do like the idea of a milestone the Promethean herself specifically wants is a good idea: a desire rooted in her Pilgrimmage to contrast with the drives rooted in her Torment and Humour; and something concrete to abandon if and when she turns away from the quest.<br /> <br /> In any case, I like this idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T08:47:52-08:00","id":355778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/353813-2ed-hack-milestones-as-aspirations?p=355759#post355759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, since milestones generate Vitriol, they imply an alchemical reaction taking place inside the Promethean - which in turn could imply she'd feel something when she approaches them, most likely a feeling she'd learn to recognise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is partially affirmed for 2ed with concept of <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/first-principles-basic-refinements/\" target=\"_blank\">Azothic Memory</a> and it's &quot;instincts&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}